    "close_notes": "Search tier intermittently unreachable by name - RESOLVED. Users could not reliably resolve the search services and occasionally reached an unrelated server. On-call first suspected the DNS appliance maintenance that had run that week and were about to open a vendor case. Before doing so we confirmed the resolver, the zone and the nameserver delegation were all healthy - the maintenance was NOT the cause. A cloud-migration re-IP earlier that month had moved the search tier to new addresses and released the old ones, but the forward zone had never been reconciled: several records still resolved to released addresses, one record collided with an address that had been reused for a different host, a newly built host that already had a live cloud interface still had its old record pointing at a released address while another new host had no record at all, and an alias pointed at a canonical name that no longer existed. We reconciled every hostname against the CMDB/IPAM host inventory AND the live cloud interfaces: repointed records to each host's live address, removed records only for hosts that had truly been decommissioned (no device and no live interface), added the records new hosts were missing, and left the correctly-migrated peer tiers and the resolver/nameservers untouched. Lesson: verify the resolver itself first, then reconcile record data to the source-of-truth inventory, and never retire a record for a host that still holds a live interface. Closed.",
    "closed_at": "2026-05-09 16:10:00",
    "description": "Search services intermittently unresolvable; DNS appliance maintenance suspected. See close notes.",
